---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Who Jack Mertens is, what he builds, and the best way to get in touch about working together."
>
  <header class="border-b border-rule pb-5">
    <h1 class="text-2xl">About</h1>
  </header>

  <div class="prose mt-10">
    <p>
      I'm Jack Mertens. I build software, and I care more about the parts that don't demo well
      — the spec written before the first commit, the test that pins down the behavior, the
      handoff that leaves someone else able to maintain the thing.
    </p>

    <h2>What I do</h2>
    <p>
      Design and build web applications end to end, from the data model through to the
      deployment. I work spec-first: the document comes before the code, and it is the thing we
      argue about while arguing is still cheap.
    </p>

    <h2>How I work</h2>
    <p>
      Test-driven where tests earn their keep. Small, reviewable changes. Plain infrastructure
      over clever infrastructure. If a dependency has to be added, it has to be justified.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      The fastest way to reach me is email. See <a href="/work/">work</a> for what I've built,
      and <a href="/writing/">writing</a> for how I think about building it.
    </p>
  </div>

  {/*
